<div class="bt">Likutay Halachos — Orach Chaim, Volume 2</div>
<div class="ht">Hilchos Birchas HaPairos — Halachah 3<br>Part 2 of 2 (§§ 7–13) — FINAL<br><span style="font-size:.95rem;font-weight:400">COMPLETE · Based on <span class="lr">LM I:37</span></span></div>

<div class="sn">§ 7 — <i>Shabbos</i>, Wine, and <i>Zikaron</i></div>

<div class="p">This is the aspect of <span class="v">"remember [zachor] the Shabbos day to sanctify it — remember it over wine."</span> <span class="h">Shabbos</span> is the aspect of <span class="h">nefesh</span> — <span class="v">"for on it He rested and was refreshed [va'yinafash]."</span> Then one merits the additional soul, and then the essential revelation of <span class="h">da'as</span>. For Torah was given on <span class="h">Shabbos</span>. The six weekdays are the aspect of body, folly — <span class="v">"the people went out and gathered — in folly,"</span> as brought. One must draw the holiness of <span class="h">Shabbos</span> onto the weekdays. The essential <span class="h">nefesh</span> and vitality of the weekdays comes from <span class="h">Shabbos</span> holiness — all six days receive vitality from the additional soul received on <span class="h">Shabbos</span>. Days following <span class="h">Shabbos</span> receive from the previous <span class="h">Shabbos</span>, etc.</div>

<div class="p">The verse warns: <span class="v">"remember the Shabbos day — remember it from the first day of the week,"</span> as our Sages said. <span class="v">"Remember"</span> specifically — for <span class="h">zikaron</span> is the aspect of <span class="h">nefesh</span>, Torah, <span class="h">da'as</span> — received in the weekdays specifically from <span class="h">Shabbos</span>. By remembering <span class="h">Shabbos</span> from the first day, one nullifies the weekdays (body) in favor of the <span class="h">nefesh</span> (<span class="h">Shabbos</span>, <span class="h">zikaron</span>).</div>

<div class="p">The essential <span class="h">Shabbos</span> remembrance from the first day is specifically through eating, as our Sages said: <span class="mx">"remember it from the first day — like Shammai the Elder who ate all his days in honor of Shabbos."</span> The essential <span class="h">zikaron</span> of <span class="h">Shabbos</span> from the weekdays — memory of the <span class="h">nefesh</span> from within the body — is through eating specifically. This is the essential honor of <span class="h">Shabbos</span> — through <span class="h">Shabbos</span> eating. Through eating, the <span class="h">nefesh</span> is elevated. Therefore it is a great <span class="h">mitzvah</span> to eat on <span class="h">Shabbos</span> — the essential <span class="h">kavod Shabbos</span>. <span class="h">Shabbos</span> is the <span class="h">nefesh</span> and Torah — on <span class="h">Shabbos</span>, the <span class="h">nefesh</span> is elevated through eating. The essential weekday <span class="h">zikaron</span> of <span class="h">Shabbos</span> is through eating — so that eating should be in the aspect of <span class="h">Shabbos</span>, elevating the <span class="h">nefesh</span> and <span class="h">zikaron</span>.</div>

<div class="p">This is <span class="v">"remember it over wine"</span> — for wine has two aspects: <span class="h">shich'chah</span> and <span class="h">zikaron</span>. <span class="v">"Lest he drink and forget the statute"</span> — forgetfulness, withdrawal of <span class="h">da'as</span>, sleep. This is when one does not merit. But when one merits, wine is the aspect of <span class="h">zikaron</span>: <span class="v">"we will remember your love more than wine"</span> — <span class="v">"they shall be remembered like the wine of Levanon."</span> This is what our Sages said about wine, called <span class="h">tirosh</span>: <span class="mx">"if he merits, he becomes a rosh [head]"</span> — <span class="h">da'as</span>, <span class="h">zikaron</span>, Torah, <span class="h">nefesh</span>. <span class="mx">"If he does not merit, he becomes rash [poor]"</span> — <span class="mx">"there is no poor but in da'as"</span> — poverty from blemished <span class="h">da'as</span> and <span class="h">nefesh</span>. Therefore on <span class="h">Shabbos</span>, when one transitions from weekdays to <span class="h">Shabbos</span>, from <span class="h">shich'chah</span> to <span class="h">zikaron</span>, one draws <span class="h">Shabbos</span> holiness through wine — <span class="v">"remember it over wine"</span> — <span class="v">"remember"</span> specifically, elevating wine from <span class="h">shich'chah</span> to <span class="h">zikaron</span>. Through this the weekdays are nullified and included in <span class="h">Shabbos</span> holiness.</div>

<div class="sn">§ 8 — Purim: Drinking Wine Subdues Amalek/<i>Shich'chah</i></div>

<div class="p">This is the intoxication of Purim — the <span class="h">mitzvah</span> to become intoxicated with wine then. For then Haman-Amalek is subdued — the aspect of <span class="h">shich'chah</span>, as brought. Therefore the Torah warns: <span class="v">"remember what Amalek did to you... do not forget"</span> — to subdue <span class="h">shich'chah</span>, the aspect of Amalek, and to elevate the <span class="h">zikaron</span>. Therefore on Purim, the <span class="h">mitzvah</span> is to become intoxicated with wine. For then wine ascends from <span class="h">shich'chah</span> to <span class="h">zikaron</span>. When wine is in holiness — ascending from <span class="h">shich'chah</span> to <span class="h">zikaron</span> — then the essential completeness is specifically through wine. For the essential completeness of <span class="h">zikaron</span> is from within <span class="h">shich'chah</span>, <span class="mx">"the advantage of light from darkness."</span> Where there is <span class="h">zikaron</span> and <span class="h">shich'chah</span> — when one merits to overcome and subdue <span class="h">shich'chah</span> (the body) and strengthen <span class="h">zikaron</span> (the <span class="h">nefesh</span>) — this is the essential completeness. This is wine in holiness.</div>

<div class="sn">§ 9 — <i>Birchas HaMazon</i> Over Wine; Three <i>Berachos</i> = Three <i>Avos</i></div>

<div class="p">This is <span class="h">Birchas HaMazon</span> over wine — so that the eating should be in the aspect of <span class="v">"and you shall remember Hashem your G-d"</span> — meriting <span class="h">zikaron</span>, <span class="h">nefesh</span>, Torah through eating. This is the three <span class="h">berachos</span> of <span class="h">Birchas HaMazon</span> corresponding to the three <span class="h">Avos</span> revealed in the world to protect through <span class="h">avira d'Eretz Yisrael</span> drawn through <span class="h">Birchas HaMazon</span> — by mentioning <span class="h">Eretz Yisrael</span> therein, which is the essence of <span class="h">Birchas HaMazon</span>: <span class="v">"and you shall bless Hashem your G-d for the land."</span> Therefore Torah is mentioned in <span class="h">Birchas HaMazon</span> — the <span class="h">nefesh</span> elevated through eating is the aspect of Torah and <span class="h">zikaron</span>.</div>

<div class="sn">§ 10 — Five Remembrances = Five Levels of the <i>Nefesh</i></div>

<div class="p">This is the aspect of the five remembrances [<span class="h">chamesh zechiros</span>]. <span class="h">Zikaron</span> is Torah, the <span class="h">nefesh</span>. Therefore there are five, corresponding to the five levels of the <span class="h">nefesh</span> — the five <span class="v">"bless Hashem, O my soul"</span> — which are the five letters <span class="h">mem-nun-tzadik-pai-chaf</span> [<span class="h">MaNTzPaCh</span>], as brought in the <span class="h">ma'amar</span>.</div>

<div class="p"><b>Remembrance of Egypt</b>: elevating the <span class="h">nefesh</span> from the exile of Egypt, which encompasses all four exiles. All exiles are called by the name Egypt, as our Sages said. In Egypt, <span class="h">da'as</span> was in exile. <span class="h">Da'as</span> is the <span class="h">nefesh</span>/<span class="h">zikaron</span>. The four exiles included in Egypt's exile correspond to the four elements from which all four exiles come. When one merits to leave all four exiles — the aspect of the Exodus — subduing the four elements — then the <span class="h">nefesh</span>/<span class="h">zikaron</span> is elevated. Then one must always remember the Exodus — guard the <span class="h">zikaron</span>, for the <span class="h">nefesh</span> has been elevated.</div>

<div class="p">This is the four cups of wine on <span class="h">Pesach</span> — corresponding to the four expressions of redemption, corresponding to the four elements that must be subdued to elevate the <span class="h">nefesh</span>/<span class="h">zikaron</span>. Then one must specifically drink wine — four cups corresponding to the four subdued elements, through which the <span class="h">nefesh</span> and <span class="h">zikaron</span> are elevated — wine in holiness.</div>

<div class="p"><b>Remembrance of Matan Torah</b>: Torah is the <span class="h">zikaron</span>.</div>

<div class="p"><b>Remembrance of Amalek</b>: to subdue <span class="h">shich'chah</span> and merit <span class="h">zikaron</span>.</div>

<div class="p"><b>Remembrance of Miriam's deed</b>: not to speak <span class="h">lashon hara</span> about Israel, for through this the <span class="h">zikaron</span> is blemished, as Rabbainu explains elsewhere — through <span class="h">lashon hara</span>, <span class="h">zikaron</span> is blemished (<span class="lr">Siman 54</span>). For <span class="h">zikaron</span> is the <span class="h">nefesh</span>, and the essential revelation of the <span class="h">nefesh</span> is through <span class="h">kavod</span>. Therefore one must be very careful to honor every Jew with all kinds of honor so the <span class="h">nefesh</span> and <span class="h">zikaron</span> are revealed. <span class="h">Lashon hara</span> is very grave — by speaking against a Jew, one disgraces a soul of Israel <span class="h">chas v'shalom</span>, and then the <span class="h">nefesh</span> cannot be revealed. This blemishes <span class="h">zikaron</span>/<span class="h">nefesh</span>, which is revealed through <span class="h">kavod</span> — the opposite of <span class="h">lashon hara</span>. Therefore one must remember Miriam's deed — <span class="v">"remember"</span> specifically — to strengthen <span class="h">zikaron</span> and subdue the <span class="h">shich'chah</span> that is the blemish of the <span class="h">nefesh</span> through <span class="h">lashon hara</span>.</div>

<div class="p"><b>Remembrance of Shabbos</b>: to draw <span class="h">zikaron</span>/<span class="h">nefesh</span> from <span class="h">Shabbos</span> to the weekdays — <span class="v">"remember it from the first day of the week,"</span> as above.</div>

<div class="sn">§ 11 — Four Fasts = Four Elements = Four Exiles</div>

<div class="p">This is the four fasts. As explained in the <span class="h">ma'amar</span>: through fasting, one subdues the body and folly — the four elements — and the <span class="h">nefesh</span> is elevated. Therefore there are four fasts corresponding to the four elements subdued through fasting. The four elements generate four exiles — the nations are to Israel as body to <span class="h">nefesh</span>, darkness to light: <span class="v">"Who separates between holy and profane, between light and darkness, between Israel and the nations, between the seventh day..."</span> Light is the <span class="h">nefesh</span>, Israel, <span class="h">Shabbos</span>. When one does not overcome the body/four elements, four exiles result — the nations prevail <span class="h">chas v'shalom</span>, the body-aspect. Therefore one fasts four fasts — to subdue the four elements/four exiles. The four fasts are for Israel's exile and the <span class="h">Bais HaMikdash's</span> destruction. By fasting and mourning over our exile from <span class="h">Eretz Yisrael</span>, we draw upon ourselves <span class="h">Eretz Yisrael</span> holiness: <span class="mx">"whoever mourns over Yerushalayim merits to see her joy."</span> Through fasting, the four elements are subdued and the <span class="h">nefesh</span> is elevated — for the essential elevation of the <span class="h">nefesh</span> is through <span class="h">Eretz Yisrael</span>.</div>

<div class="sn">§ 12 — Hold the Fruit in the Right Hand</div>

<div class="p">Therefore when blessing on a fruit, one must hold it in the right hand. This is the elevation of the <span class="h">nefesh</span> through subduing the body's desires — through which <span class="h">chesed</span> is drawn. Therefore one holds the fruit in the right hand, which is <span class="h">chesed</span>.</div>

<div class="sn">§ 13 — Wine Libations at the <i>Korban</i>: From <i>Behaima</i> to <i>Adam</i></div>

<div class="p">This is the wine libations at the time of the <span class="h">korban</span> — when one elevates from <span class="h">behaima</span> to <span class="h">adam</span>, which is the essential aspect of the <span class="h">korban</span>. Then wine is poured as a libation — to elevate wine from <span class="h">shich'chah</span> to <span class="h">zikaron</span>: <span class="v">"they shall be remembered like the wine of Levanon"</span> — the Targum: <span class="mx">"like the remembrance of trumpeting... over aged wine that is poured as libation"</span> (Hoshea 14). For <span class="h">shich'chah</span> and <span class="h">zikaron</span> are the aspects of <span class="h">adam</span> and <span class="h">behaima</span>, as explained in the <span class="h">ma'amar</span>. At the time of the wine libation, they sounded the trumpets — the aspect of <span class="h">zikaron</span>: <span class="v">"and you shall sound the trumpets over your burnt offerings... and it shall be a remembrance for you."</span></div>

<div class="ts">
<div class="sh">✦ Summary — Birchas HaPairos Halachah 3 ✦</div>
<p style="margin-bottom:.8rem"><strong>Core teaching</strong> (<span class="lr">LM I:37</span>): Body/soul = <em>behaima</em>/<em>adam</em> = forgetfulness/memory = folly/Torah. Subdue the body through fasting → <em>chesed</em> → <em>nefesh</em> elevated through <em>avira d'Eretz Yisrael</em> and breath of schoolchildren.</p>
<p style="margin-bottom:.8rem"><strong>§§1-2</strong>: <em>Birchos hanehenin</em> elevate reincarnated <em>nefashos</em>. Essential <em>berachah</em> = <em>avira d'Eretz Yisrael</em>. Money = root of <em>nefesh</em> → <em>nezikin</em> and <em>tzedakah</em> both elevate the <em>nefesh</em>.</p>
<p style="margin-bottom:.8rem"><strong>§§3-4</strong>: Precedence in <em>berachos</em> through <em>kavod</em>. Seven Species of <em>Eretz Yisrael</em> = highest souls. <em>Kazayis</em> (olive) = body and soul; oil = memory from within forgetfulness.</p>
<p style="margin-bottom:.8rem"><strong>§§5-6</strong>: Eating a <em>kazayis</em> requires final <em>berachah</em> to guard <em>zikaron</em>. First <em>berachah</em> has no minimum — initial revelation of <em>da'as</em> is beyond measure.</p>
<p style="margin-bottom:.8rem"><strong>§§7-8</strong>: <em>Shabbos</em> <em>kiddush</em> over wine = <em>zikaron</em> from <em>shich'chah</em>. Purim intoxication = subduing Amalek/<em>shich'chah</em> through wine in holiness.</p>
<p style="margin-bottom:.8rem"><strong>§§9-10</strong>: Three <em>berachos</em> of <em>BhM</em> = three <em>Avos</em>. Five remembrances = five levels of <em>nefesh</em>. <em>Lashon hara</em> blemishes <em>zikaron</em> (opposite of <em>kavod</em>).</p>
<p style="margin-bottom:.8rem"><strong>§§11-13</strong>: Four fasts = four elements/exiles. Hold fruit in right hand = <em>chesed</em>. Wine libations with trumpets = elevating from <em>behaima</em> to <em>adam</em>, <em>shich'chah</em> to <em>zikaron</em>.</p>
</div>

